{"id": "EUVD-2026-108761", "enisaUuid": "78fea2e5-4aab-3360-a92f-2c49b5fe7d32", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncxgb4/ch_ktls: disable softirqs around tid_list erases\n\nchcr_ktls_cpl_act_open_rpl() inserts into tid_list from the receive path\nusing xa_insert_bh().  The array is shared by the adapter's connections\nand initialized with XA_FLAGS_LOCK_BH.  However, chcr_ktls_dev_del() and\nthe chcr_ktls_dev_add() error path use xa_erase(), which takes the XArray\nlock without disabling softirqs.\n\nWhen cleanup runs with softirqs enabled, a receive softirq for another\nconnection on the same CPU can interrupt the erase and spin on the lock\nheld by the interrupted task.  Use xa_erase_bh() at both sites to match\nthe insertion path.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:19:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:19:37", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8739f06e3f82cd715f7dd10ab24029ed881efc90", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bcf97573d44e277b1744d7f1226f665aa0ccc599", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7110c7f70c59eb7924e79853bcc00e2a026662e6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bea736a2b8c6da5b1078badf1206541b5404250f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4c9dc0faca98084922caeb689579d338cf3e1c29"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98967"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "10f73c7e-5362-3049-b14b-608c9a4b6654", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "39687824-53f4-39d2-beb6-1e47a49e6453", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "65e302a9bd57b62872040d57eea1201562a7cbb2 <7110c7f70c59eb7924e79853bcc00e2a026662e6"}, {"id": "4dfc81c4-ae93-3e65-a118-eccaeb12ab14", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "65e302a9bd57b62872040d57eea1201562a7cbb2 <bea736a2b8c6da5b1078badf1206541b5404250f"}, {"id": "502b7d25-76d6-3a3d-8ab3-60ce89649abc", "product": 